Good Morning!

Sunny Sunday greetings from South Florida, where we have enjoyed a warm but=
 dry weather week.  Back in the days when I was doing New Student Orientati=
on on the FAU campus, it managed to rain nearly every day, so I am not sure=
 how we got so lucky this week.

As we pause on this Father's Day Sunday to honor fathers everywhere, please=
 take a moment to honor the memory of fathers who are no longer with us.  H=
ere is my Dad, Dr. Milton W. Sanderson, 1910-2012.


Our jokes today, stolen as usual, are dedicated to the Office of Appreciati=
ve Education staff and interns for the outstanding institute we just hosted=
.  GREAT job, team!

Keep smiling.........................ss

***************************************************************************=
***********************************



Mikey's Funnies:

Little Dewey was brought to Dr. Dr. Mike Wilson  because he hadn't eaten an=
ything for days. Dr. Wilson offered him all the goodies he could think of. =
No luck. He tried a little scolding. It didn't work. A little pleading, to =
no avail.

Finally he sat down, faced the boy, looked him in the eye. He said, "Look y=
oung man, if you can be stubborn, so can I. You're not going anywhere until=
 you eat something. You can have whatever you want, but only after you have=
 eaten will you leave."

Dewey just sat and glared for some time, then said, "OK. I'll eat but I hav=
e some conditions. First, I'll have exactly what I want and exactly how I w=
ant it and second you'll share with me."

Dr. Wilson was OK with this. He asked the child what he'd like. "Worms!" sa=
id Dewey.

Dr. Wilson was horrified but didn't want to back out and seem like a loser.=
 So, he ordered a plate of worms to be brought in. "Not that many, just one=
," yelled Dewey as he saw the plate.

So, everything other than one worm was removed. Dewey then demanded that th=
e single worm be cut into two pieces and then Dr. Wilson eat half. Dr. Wils=
on went through the worst ordeal of his life, and after finishing, barely m=
anaging to keep his cool, said, "OK, now eat!"

Dewey refused as he sobbed, "No way! You ate my half!"





Mikey's Funnies:

A customer asked his barber, "When would be the best time to bring in my tw=
o-year-old son?"

Without hesitation, the barber answered, "When he's four."




The Good Clean Fun List:

A Frenchman walks into a bar with a parrot perched on his shoulder. "Wow," =
says the bartended, "that's pretty cool, where'd you get him?"

"Oh, him?" Says the parrot, "I found him in France, There's millions more o=
ver there."




Mikey's Funnies:

Kathy and Rachel were chatting about her upcoming first year at Central Mic=
higan University. Rachel was excited about Central, as other members of the=
 family had also gone there..

"What would you like to take when you attend college?" Kathy asked.

After giving it some thought and glancing around the kitchen, Rachel replie=
d, "The refrigerator, if you can get along without it."




A Joke A Day:

When a squirrel slipped into my house, I did the logical thing: I panicked =
and called my father.

"How do you get a squirrel out of a basement?" I shrieked.

Dad advised me to leave a trail of peanut butter and crackers from the base=
ment to the outside. It worked-the squirrel ate his way out of the house. U=
nfortunately, he passed another squirrel eating his way in.




